N|            keeps walking along with Shcherbina.                                    
O|
N|            And the pets... and the KGB... keep following.                          
O|
S|       320  INT. POLISSYA HOTEL - LOBBY BAR - NIGHT                       320       
O|
N|            Legasov, returning, crosses through the now-abandoned lobby,            
N|            then sees:                                                              
O|
N|            KHOMYUK alone at the lobby bar, papers spread out around                
N|            her. Scribbling calculations. A bottle of vodka and a glass.            
O|
N|            He hesitates. Makes a silent decision. Then crosses over and            
N|            takes a seat near her at the bar.                                       
O|
N|            She glances up at him from her work, then eyes back down to             
N|            her calculations. But she slides a spectrograph page over to            
N|            him from the top of her papers. Keeps her eyes on her work              
N|            as she talks.                                                           
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
U|                         You've seen that? The fuel is melting                      
U|                         faster than we expected. The pad--                         
O|
C|                                     LEGASOV                                        
U|                         I know. I have a plan.                                     
O|
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
U|                         Heat exchanger, I hope.                                    
C|                                     LEGASOV                                        
U|                         Yes.                                                       
P|                               (her equations)                                      
U|                         There's something I've wanted to ask                       
U|                         you, Comrade. But I see you've been                        
U|                         asking it yourself.                                        
O|
N|            She finally slams her pencil down. Beyond frustrated. The               
N|            anger of a relentless mind facing an unsolvable puzzle.                 
O|
O|
O|                                                                     19.            
O|
