N|            A group of forty-five MINERS on break. Vodka. Cigarettes.               
N|            Behind them, conveyor belts and hoppers. Bulldozers and                 
N|            dust. Rolling hills pierced by cart tracks.                             
N|            These men are hard. Blackened faces. Blackened lungs. Young             
N|            and old. Thick bellies. Tough muscle. But right now...                  
O|
C|                                     OLD MINER                                      
U|                         Wait wait I have one, I have one...                        
U|                         so every Friday, Maxim The Factory                         
U|                         Guard sees Yaroslav The Worker coming                      
U|                         out of the factory with a wheelbarrow                      
U|                         full of hay. And each time, Maxim                          
U|                         looks through the hay to see what                          
U|                         Yaroslav's stealing, but he never                          
U|                         finds anything. They do this for                           
U|                         thirty years until Maxim says,                             
U|                         "Yaroslav, I'm retiring. It's my last                      
U|                         day. I promise-- I won't tell anyone,                      
U|                         but I have to know. What have you                          
U|                         been stealing?" And Yaroslav says--                        
