N|            Vasily instantly closes his eyes in pain. Lyudmilla quickly             
N|            returns to his side, and places special, bandaged DARKENED              
N|            LENSES gently over his eyes.                                            
O|
N|            He waits for the pain to subside. Then...                               
C|                                     VASILY                                         
U|                         What do you see? Tell me everything.                       
O|
N|            She turns slowly back to the window. From here, the only                
N|            view is a dismal array of brutally ugly apartment buildings,            
N|            and a grim highway just beyond.                                         
O|
C|                                     LYUDMILLA                                      
U|                         I see the Red Square from here. The                        
U|                         Kremlin, the Mausoleum, Spasskaya                          
U|                         Tower...                                                   
O|
N|            He nods. Pleased.                                                       
C|                                     VASILY                                         
U|                         Saint Basil's?                                             
O|
C|                                     LYUDMILLA                                      
U|                         Yes. It's beautiful.                                       
O|
C|                                     VASILY                                         
U|                         You see? I told you I'd show you                           
U|                         Moscow one day. I told you.                                
O|
N|            She walks back to him. Sits down. Gently takes his hand. The            
N|            flesh hangs strangely from his bones, as if it's separating.            
C|                                     LYUDMILLA                                      
U|                         Thank you, my love.                                        
O|
N,G|            BEHIND HER - through the interior window facing the hospital            
N,G|            hallway, we see a figure in PROTECTIVE GEAR passing by...               
O|
O|
O|                                                                     26.            
O|
S|       325  INT. HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS                                     325       
O|
N|            KHOMYUK strides down the hallway in medical clothing. Rubber            
N|            gloves. Rubber booties. Sleeves and pants cuffs tucked in.              
N|            In her hand, a notebook and pen. She stops in front of a                
N|            door, then takes a breath, and raises a cloth face-mask in              
N|            place to cover her nose and mouth.                                      
O|
N|            She opens the door.                                                     
O|
N,G|            INSIDE THE HOSPITAL ROOM - a man stands in a hospital gown,             
N,G|            his back to us, staring out the window. He turns slowly at              
N|            the sound of the door.                                                  
O|
N|            It's DYATLOV. His hair is now missing in patches. His                   
N|            eyebrows are gone. But otherwise-- he seems oddly fine. No              
N|            trace of the morphine delirium we saw before.                           
N|            He gestures to an uneaten tray of food. Contemptous.                    
O|
C|                                     DYATLOV                                        
U|                         I'm not eating that. It's shit. Bring                      
U|                         me something else.                                         
O|
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
U|                         I'm not a nurse, Comrade Dyatlov. I'm                      
U|                         a nuclear physicist.                                       
O|
N|            Oh really? Her? A sneer, then:                                          
C|                                     DYATLOV                                        
U|                         Well then, Comrade Nuclear Physicist,                      
U|                         unless you happen to have a butter                         
U|                         and caviar sandwich with you, you can                      
U|                         get the fuck out of my room.                               
O|
