N|            off the table.                                                          
O|
O|
O|                                                                     30.            
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         We'll start now. I don't want my men                       
U|                         here one second more than they have                        
U|                         to be.                                                     
N|            He stares at his gas mask for a moment.                                 
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         If these worked, you'd be wearing                          
U|                         them.                                                      
O|
N|            He tosses the gas mask back on the table, and exits.                    
O|
T|                                                            CUT TO:                 
O|
S|       328  NEAR PITCH BLACK                                              328       
N|            The sound of muffled men shouting to each other. A heavy                
N|            RATTLE of metal...                                                      
O|
M|            TITLE:                                                                  
O|
M|                                     MAY 6, 1986                                    
O|
N|            And then a MINER shifts his head to UNBLOCK the lights                  
N,G|            behind him, and now we see him and a coworker PUSHING a MINE            
N|            CART full of dirt around a CORNER and--                                 
O|
S|       329  EXT. REACTOR SITE - DAY - MOMENTS LATER                       329       
N|            They EMERGE from the MOUTH of the tunnel shaft, and quickly             
N|            TILT the minecart to empty the dirt.                                    
O|
N|            They wear simple white uniforms, and simple white caps, much            
N|            in the style of the reactor control room workers. But these             
N|            men are covered in dirt. And dripping in sweat.                         
O|
N|            There is a SIGN nailed to the side of the shaft entrance...             
N|            yellow Cyrillic lettering on a piece of brown plywood.                  
O|
N|            SUBTITLE: Comrades: our goal, 24/7, is to advance the tunnel            
N|            by 13 metres each day                                                   
N|            GLUKHOV emerges from the tunnel, right behind them. Jumps up            
N|            out of the entrance trench.                                             
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         Quickly. Back in. You two! Behind                          
U|                         them.                                                      
O|                                     (MORE)                                         
O|
O|
O|                                                                     31.            
O|
C,E|                                     GLUKHOV (cont'd)                               
P|                               (to another miner)                                   
U|                         Iosif, get another spool of wire, and                      
U|                         tell group three to switch with two.                       
O|
N|            They move quickly, and without care. Jumping down into the              
N|            dirt. Wiping the sweaty dust from their faces. No one is                
N|            wearing a mask.                                                         
N|            Glukhov looks up at the SUN. It's beating down, and it's not            
N|            even noon yet.                                                          
O|
N|            He walks over to a crude, brown INTERCOM BOX set on top of              
N|            some SANDBAGS. Pushes a button on it twice. It emits two                
N|            signal tones. Bweee bwee... then we hear a VOICE, crackling             
N|            through the tiny speaker.                                               
O|
C,E|                                     MINER (INTERCOM)                               
U|                         Yes?                                                       
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         What is it up to?                                          
O|
C,E|                                     MINER (INTERCOM)                               
U|                         Fifty.                                                     
O|
N|            Glukhov hangs his head in frustration. Then sees:                       
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         Hey. HEY, you!                                             
O|
N|            PIKALOV, issuing commands to his radiometrists, looks over              
N|            to see: this short, angry miner MARCHING toward him.                    
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         We need fans. Thirty or forty.                             
O|
C|                                     PIKALOV                                        
U|                         For what purpose?                                          
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         What do you mean? What purpose? To                         
U|                         dig your fucking tunnel, what else?                        
O|
N|            One of Pikalov's men reacts, angrily, but Glukhov jabs his              
N|            finger in the air at the soldier.                                       
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         Who's talking to you? Who?                                 
O|
N|            Pikalov raises a hand. Gets in between them.                            
O|
C|                                     PIKALOV                                        
U|                         Comrades--                                                 
O|
O|
O|                                                                     32.            
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
P|                               (back to Pikalov)                                    
U|                         It's 50 degrees down there. We can't                       
U|                         breathe with the masks, we can't                           
U|                         breathe without the masks. It's an                         
U|                         oven. We need ventilation.                                 
C|                                     PIKALOV                                        
U|                         Fans will put dust in the air. The                         
U|                         dust will go in your lungs.                                
O|
C|                                     GLUKHOV                                        
U|                         I've been filling my lungs with dust                       
U|                         for twenty years.                                          
O|
C|                                     PIKALOV                                        
U|                         Not this dust. I'm sorry. But for                          
U|                         your own good-- no fans.                                   
