O|
G,T|            We LOWER DOWN - INTO THE EARTH itself... until we come to:              
O|
S|       330  INT. THE TUNNEL - NOW                                         330       
O|
N|            A cramped shaft, dimly lit by bulb strung along swales of               
N|            electrical cord.                                                        
O|
N|            Five miners are jammed against each other like rats in a                
N|            nest, stooped over in the low tunnel, PICKING and SHOVELING             
N|            into the earth as fast as they can manage.                              
N|            The heat is intense. Rippling the air in spots. They drip               
N|            sweat, but they keep working.                                           
O|
N|            Gritting teeth. Muscles burning. And even without fans, the             
N|            DUST swirls around them... it SHIMMERS in front of the                  
N|            lights... and we can literally see them inhaling it...                  
O|
N,T,G|            A miner swings his PICK right at us, and we cut to:                     
O|
S|       331  INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - DAY                                      331       
N,I|            LEONID TOPTUNOV, the young control room engineer, lies in a             
N|            bed. Most of his hair is gone. Bits of his mustache remain              
N|            in small patches. His body looks just as bad as Ignatenko's.            
N|            Discolored. Swollen. Thousand yard stare.                               
O|
N|            He barely glances as KHOMYUK enters the room. Then back to              
N|            the thousand yard stare.                                                
O|
O|
O|                                                                     33.            
O|
N|            She moves the chair back a few feet from his bed to maintain            
N|            a safer distance, and sits. Still in full protection, mask              
N|            covering her mouth. Notebook open in her lap. Pen poised.               
O|
N|            She hesitates. Difficult to interrogate someone who is dying            
N|            in front of your eyes. But no choice.                                   
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
U|                         My name is Ulana Khomyuk. I am a                           
U|                         nuclear physicist working with the                         
U|                         Chernobyl Commission. I want you to                        
U|                         tell me everything that happened the                       
U|                         night of the accident. Is that all                         
U|                         right?                                                     
O|
C|                                     TOPTUNOV                                       
P|                               (hurts to speak)                                     
U|                         Yes. I want to tell.                                       
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
P|                               (reluctantly)                                        
U|                         Alright. Your official title was--                         
O|
C|                                     TOPTUNOV                                       
P|                               (a strange pride)                                    
U|                         My name is Leonid Fedorovych                               
U|                         Toptunov. I am the Senior Reactor                          
U|                         Control Chief Engineer at Chernobyl                        
U|                         Nuclear Power Plant.                                       
O|
N|            She stops writing. Surprised.                                           
C|                                     KHOMYUK                                        
U|                         Senior engineer? How old are you?                          
O|
N|            He slowly turns his head to face her.                                   
O|
C|                                     TOPTUNOV                                       
U|                         I'm 25.                                                    
O|
N|            And now BLOOD begins leaking from his nostrils. Steady                  
N|            rivulets... coming out too easily. Coming out too thin.                 
O|
N|            Khomyuk crosses to the bedside table, picks up some cotton              
N|            gauze, leans over Toptunov, and presses it gently to his                
N|            nose.                                                                   
N|            They're looking straight at each other.                                 
O|
N|            Her face covered by a mask. His face covered by the gauze.              
N|            Nothing revealed but eyes gazing into eyes.                             
O|
O|
O|                                                                     34.            
O|
S|       332  EXT. HOSPITAL HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS                            332       
O|
N|            The long hallway - then a BLOND MAN steps into view. 30's,              
N|            mustache. Rolling a sucking candy around in his mouth. He               
N|            looks around. Oddly out of place, and yet zero emotion.                 
N|            Just a dead look. It should be quite clear what he is.                  
O|
N|            He steps out of the way as ORDERLIES come by, wheeling a                
N|            GURNEY - with VASILY, the dark lenses shielding his eyes                
N|            from the light. Lyudmilla follows right behind.                         
O|
N,G|            We move WITH THEM, leaving the Blond Man behind.                        
O|
C|                                     VASILY                                         
P|                               (scared)                                             
U|                         Lyusya...?                                                 
C|                                     LYUDMILLA                                      
U|                         I'm here.                                                  
O|
N|            They round a corner, and move toward a single room at the               
N|            end of the hallway. Double doors.                                       
O|
N|            VETROVA emerges from the room. Visible behind her, in the               
N,G|            center of the room, we see heavy, CLEAR PLASTIC SHEETING                
N|            dangling in overlapping strips from the ceiling.                        
O|
