O|
C|                                     VETROVA                                        
U|                         I did. Thirty minutes, I said!                             
O|
C|                                     LYUDMILLA                                      
P|                               (anger)                                              
U|                         Well where have you been? When he's                        
U|                         in pain? When his sores stick to his                       
U|                         gown? When he soils himself five                           
U|                         times a night-- I've been taking care                      
U|                         of him. Where have you been?                               
N|            Vetrova draws on every ounce of calm she has.                           
O|
O|
O|                                                                     35.            
O|
C|                                     VETROVA                                        
U|                         I have been in the north and west                          
U|                         wing where there are dozens of                             
U|                         patients from Chernobyl, exactly like                      
